 "poem": "Though, in a little walk by adriatic,\nThe dust of the marches may be believed;\nBut I cannot tell you how much perhaps\nI loved those mountains in a Shakespeare.\nIII - Old Island and Lagoon. Again.\n'T is rather hard to write myself again,\nFor there's something of a poet's disdain,\nWhen, in the course of life, I have never\nRecalled the laurel 'twixt my fingers.\nAs for 'the sublime,' that thing, indeed,\nIs one of the wonders of the history,\nIf not of men, at least of age, even,",
